{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347706-cutting-the-knot-style-peach","id":1347706,"title":"Cutting the Knot Style [PEACH]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-11T10:17:48-08:00","id":1347706,"title":"Cutting the Knot Style [PEACH]","content":"Cutting the Knot Style<br /> Weapons: Cutting the Knot style can be practiced with the Kama, Seven-Section Staff, Scythe, or unarmed.<br /> Armor: Cutting the Knot Style may not be practiced in armor: None<br /> <br /> <b>Direction Means Nothing</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mastery<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>None<br /> The martial artist weaves back and forth around attacks. No matter where the enemy strikes, a wall is there, blocking. Even in the absence of a wall, the ground itself is somehow in the way of an enemy\u2019s blows.<br /> This supplements a take cover action. You may take cover without any cover, counting it as light cover, or count light cover as heavy, or gain +1 defense while in heavy cover. You count cover as it\u2019s actual strength for the purposes of attacking enemies at close range. This charm ends if you leave cover.<br /> Mastery: Ignore any penalties for flurrying the take cover action.<br /> <br /> <b>Single Path Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>None<br /> True knowledge takes time, and understanding. The scholar knows that it is better to think through a problem to get the right answer than to rush things.<br /> An aimed attack gains +(lore) dice non-charm dice instead of +3. If they are in cover, reduce the strength by 1 step, including if you are in cover while they are at close range. <br /> <br /> <b>Perception Evading Pursuit</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mastery<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>None<br /> Chasing a scholar is like chasing an idea \u2013 it matters less how fast one is than if you are even running in the right direction.<br /> This supplements a movement action, or an attempt to resist a movement action. Enemies with lower initiative than you have a \u2013(lore/2, round up) penalty on their roll. In Gordian Knot Form, count based on your boosted initiative.<br /> Mastery: If you succeed, all enemies opposing you lose (lore/2, round down) initiative<br /> <br /> <b>Cutting the Knot Form</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Form<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Direction Means Nothing, Single Path Strike, Perception Evading Pursuit<br /> You may make attacks out to short range. If you do so, that enemy treats you as if you were in close range until your next turn.<br /> You may delay without initiative penalty.<br /> Treat your initiative as (lore) higher for the purposes of turn order.<br /> Reflexive: <br /> <br /> <b>Space-Filling Knives Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mastery, Terrestrial, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Turn<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Cutting the Knot Form<br /> The martial artist assumes a defensive stance, weapons spinning such that no matter where her enemy strikes, a blade is there to snatch if from the air.<br /> Ignore onslaught penalties until your next turn. Attacks which miss you inflict 1 point of onslaught penalty on them, you may pay up to (amount they missed by) initiative to deal that many dice of hardness-ignoring damage (type is based on a weapon you wield)<br /> Terrestrial: Damage max is (essence)<br /> Mastery: You may flurry this with a defend other action.<br /> <br /> <b>Timeless Path Intersection</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mastery<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Cutting the Knot Form<br /> A good scholar writes down her insights, so that she might use them again. So too does a warrior remember how she previously landed her strikes.<br /> This supplements an aim action. The action benefits your next two attacks on your next two turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Twisted Perception Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m, 1i; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mastery, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Turn<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Timeless Path Intersection<br /> Supplements an aimed attack. If it hits, the enemy has a -1 penalty to defense, and -1 to all dice rolls per 10 on the damage roll until the end of your next turn.<br /> Mastery: Add up to 3 extra successes to damage for decisive, or add 3 post-soak damage to a withering attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Infinite Possibility Onslaught</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Terrestrial, Decisive-Only, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Cutting the Knot Form<br /> Make up to (Lore) decisive attacks against a single person, splitting your initiative equally between them, round up. After hitting with any attack, you may end this early. If you do, for every extra success on the attack roll, convert one die of damage to an automatic success. You do not lose initiative for hitting or missing until the end of the series, at which point you reset to base initiative if any hit, or lose initiative for each attack you made if all missed (lose 2i for attacks which carried 10 or less initiative, 3i for attacks which carried 11 or more)<br /> Terrestrial: Make (lesser of Lore and Essence) attacks.<br /> Mastery: All of the attacks are considered a single attack for the purposes of using up aiming. <br /> <br /> <b>Perfect Arc Attack</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Terrestrial, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Infinite Possibility Onslaught<br /> Make a decisive attack against all enemies in close range of you. In the form, you may target every enemy within short range, granting them the same ability to attack you as normal. Divide your initiative as evenly as possible between everyone hit.<br /> Terrestrial: You must aim before making this attack, and do not gain the ordinary benefits of aiming. If you aim twice before this attack, you gain the ordinary benefits of aiming from one of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Arbitrary Omphalos Point</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b><br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Space-Filling Knives Stance, Twisted Perception Strike, Perfect Arc Attack<br /> Every map has a center, but this is simply chosen by the whims of the mapmaker. The imperial mountain has no more claim to this title than the ground beneath your feet.<br /> Any time a distance to or from you is measured, you may have it count as one range band less. This lets you attack at range and defend other, interfere with the accuracy of withering archery attacks, contest disengage attempts at short range, or similar. If you use the form to attack an enemy at medium range, they still count as being at close range of you until your next turn.<br /> You cannot move a range band without losing this effect.<br /> At the start of your turn, you may take one of the following actions reflexively: Enter Cover, Defend Other, or a Miscellaneous Action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T05:14:36-08:00","id":1347866,"title":"","content":"I love the flavor of striking anything from anywhere, but I have trouble figuring out how much punch the style has in terms of raw power. What would you say is the most powerful attack you could do with the style?<br /> <br /> One other thing I'm wondering - narratively speaking, what exactly happens when an enemy attacks you from short range because you count as close range from them? They attack a sort of afterimage or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T05:31:23-08:00","id":1347868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347706-cutting-the-knot-style-peach?p=1347866#post1347866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the flavor of striking anything from anywhere, but I have trouble figuring out how much punch the style has in terms of raw power. What would you say is the most powerful attack you could do with the style?<br /> <br /> One other thing I'm wondering - narratively speaking, what exactly happens when an enemy attacks you from short range because you count as close range from them? They attack a sort of afterimage or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most powerful attack assuming mastery might be something like:<br /> Aim (Timeless Path Intersection)<br /> Twisted Perception Strike (Withering, using Single Path Strike) to impose penalties.<br /> On the next round, delay so the penalties also encompass their turn this round.<br /> Infinite Possibility Onslaught (Singe Path Strike). Ideally one of your attacks will have extra successes (aim bonus, Twisted Perspective Strike gives penalties, onslaught penalties, they can't afford to spend motes on every defense), and you can have that one deal a bunch of damage.<br /> <br /> The flavor of the form is supposed to be space-warping - you're shortening the distance between you and them to attack, but doing so also shortens the distance for them to attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T06:04:37-08:00","id":1347872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347706-cutting-the-knot-style-peach?p=1347868#post1347868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most powerful attack assuming mastery might be something like:<br /> Aim (Timeless Path Intersection)<br /> Twisted Perception Strike (Withering, using Single Path Strike) to impose penalties.<br /> On the next round, delay so the penalties also encompass their turn this round.<br /> Infinite Possibility Onslaught (Singe Path Strike). Ideally one of your attacks will have extra successes (aim bonus, Twisted Perspective Strike gives penalties, onslaught penalties, they can't afford to spend motes on every defense), and you can have that one deal a bunch of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that does seem to pack a punch. The style looks good, the only thing I'd be careful about is how its Charms might interact with other styles given it has many unusual effects. That said I don't know Martial Arts Charms well enough to say whether this style breaks anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347706-cutting-the-knot-style-peach?p=1347868#post1347868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flavor of the form is supposed to be space-warping - you're shortening the distance between you and them to attack, but doing so also shortens the distance for them to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that look like to an onlooker? Does Arbitrary Omphalos Point turn the whole battlefield into a surreal kaleidoscope of stretched out combatants?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T04:54:51-08:00","id":1348228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1347706-cutting-the-knot-style-peach?p=1347872#post1347872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, that does seem to pack a punch. The style looks good, the only thing I'd be careful about is how its Charms might interact with other styles given it has many unusual effects. That said I don't know Martial Arts Charms well enough to say whether this style breaks anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> How would that look like to an onlooker? Does Arbitrary Omphalos Point turn the whole battlefield into a surreal kaleidoscope of stretched out combatants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't much thought about how it looks to an onlooker, but yes, I'd imagine pretty bizarre. Probably a mixture of people and things being stretched out, and movement being unnaturally fast? I think a lot of the stretching only happens when people use it, so less a person consistently twisted and more a person blurring so they take up the entirety of a 30ft line for a second, then resolving at one side or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}